          "value": "The user has a history of creative engagement with music, including remixing, composing original music, exploring genres and cultural significance, attending live performances, and making playlists. They have expressed a strong desire to focus on original compositions and personal projects, stepping back from remixing to develop their unique artistic voice. They have also tried researching historical music trends in 2020 but found it tedious and overwhelming, preferring less structured exploration. They have felt unsatisfied with passive consumption (e.g., a documentary that skimmed over the artistic process) and recognized the importance of personal creation and emotional connection over technical analysis. They have committed to investing time in original music creation and aligning their pursuits with what truly inspires them. Additionally, they have experienced creative friction in a band setting, leading to a desire for more autonomy. They have enrolled in an audio production workshop to deepen technical skills, launched a podcast on fusion of traditional and electronic music, explored audio production but found it too technical, and blended field recordings of nature with music. They also recall an early positive experience with digital remixing in 2010.",
